2	 * The step machine behind the builder's progress display.
3	 *
4	 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
5	 * WHY THIS IS A PURE REDUCER
6	 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
7	 * `AIProgress` is only honest if every step change is caused by something that
8	 * actually happened. Keeping the mapping here — with no timers, no setTimeout
9	 * and no access to the clock — makes that structurally true rather than a
10	 * promise in a comment: this module CANNOT advance a step on its own, because
11	 * the only way to move it is to hand it a signal.
12	 *
13	 * The chat panel's step list, the initial-build overlay and the veil over the
14	 * preview all render from one `BuildRun`, so the three of them cannot disagree
15	 * about what is happening.
16	 *
17	 * This is deliberately the same shape as the reducer behind the create flow
18	 * (app/(portal)/dashboard/new/build-steps.ts). The two surfaces show a customer
19	 * the same product and must not narrate a build in two different vocabularies.
20	 * The step LABELS differ, because an edit is not a create and "Writing your
21	 * site's files" is the wrong sentence for someone who asked to change a button.
22	 *
23	 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
24	 * THE REAL SSE VOCABULARY OF /api/generate  (audited against route.ts,
25	 * lib/agent.ts, lib/agent-sdk.ts and lib/build-narration.ts)
26	 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
27	 * `app/api/generate/route.ts` writes `data: <json>\n\n` frames. Exactly six
28	 * event shapes ever reach the client:
29	 *
30	 *   { type: "text",     text }                 assistant prose deltas
31	 *   { type: "progress", text }                 one narrated tool call
32	 *   { type: "status",   text }                 a phase the server names itself
33	 *   { type: "file",     path, action }         a source file was written/deleted
34	 *   { type: "done",     credits, remaining, filesWritten, buildId,
35	 *                       repairAttempts, repairWaived, waivedCredits }
36	 *   { type: "error",    message }
37	 *
38	 * A seventh, { type: "usage", … }, is produced by the agent and consumed
39	 * SERVER-SIDE for billing. It is never forwarded, so the client cannot show a
40	 * live spend readout during a build and nothing here pretends it can. The
41	 * charge is known once, on `done`.
42	 *
43	 * The two text channels are not free-form. Their producers are enumerable:
44	 *
45	 *   `progress` — narrateTool() in lib/build-narration.ts, one line per real
46	 *     tool call, with consecutive duplicates collapsed by the route:
47	 *       "Writing <thing>" / "Writing a file"      (Write, write_file)
48	 *       "Updating <thing>" / "Making an edit"     (Edit)
49	 *       "Removing <thing>" / "Removing a file"    (delete_file)
50	 *       "Looking through the project"             (Read, Glob, Grep — sdk)
51	 *       "Running a command"                       (Bash — sdk)
52	 *     plus two emitted directly:
53	 *       "Picking out icons and artwork"           (lib/agent.ts, find_assets)
54	 *       "Compiling the site"                      (route, before buildSite();
55	 *                                                  bypasses the dedupe)
56	 *
57	 *   `status` — only two producers:
58	 *       "Building your site…" / "Applying your changes…"  (sdk engine, once)
59	 *       "Build didn't compile — fixing it…"               (route, per repair;
60	 *                                                          MAX_BUILD_ATTEMPTS
61	 *                                                          is 2, so at most one)
62	 *
63	 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
64	 * WHAT THAT VOCABULARY CAN AND CANNOT SUPPORT
65	 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
66	 * There is no "planning" marker and no "designing" marker, and nothing can
67	 * separate layout work from copy work — a write to src/components/Hero.tsx is
68	 * one `file` event whether the model was laying out a grid or writing the
69	 * headline. A longer list would mean inventing the extra entries, and a step
70	 * that lights up because four seconds elapsed is exactly the fake this exists
71	 * to remove. So: FOUR steps, each entered or completed by a specific
72	 * observable fact.
73	 *
74	 *   0 sending    done when POST /api/generate answers 200 with a body — which
75	 *                means the kill switch, the balance, the spend cap and the
76	 *                rate limit all passed and a Build row exists
77	 *   1 thinking   done at the first evidence of a WRITE (a `file` event, or a
78	 *                narrateTool line from the Write/Edit/delete branch)
79	 *   2 writing    done when the route sends progress "Compiling the site"
80	 *   3 compiling  done on `done`
81	 *
82	 * The list can move BACKWARD. `status: "Build didn't compile — fixing it…"`
83	 * returns the active step to `writing` and increments a real counter, because
84	 * that is what the server just did — the files are being changed again. An
85	 * `error` freezes the list and marks the step it died on as failed. A stream
86	 * that closes with neither `done` nor `error` is a dropped connection and is
87	 * never reported as a finish.
88	 */
